        {
          "id": "artificial-intelligence-and-machine-learning-3-pbcst304-mModule 4-t29",
          "title": "Project Suggestion: Library Management System using OOP and SQL - Design and implement the Circulation function in a Library Management System using Object-Oriented Programming principles in Java and limited use of SQL. Class Design: Book (title, author, ISBN, genre, status), User (user ID, name, contact information, borrowed books list), Library (lists of books and users), Librarian (inherits from User, adds/removes books, manages users), BorrowTransaction (transaction ID, book, user, borrow date, return date). Functionalities: Book Management (add, remove, update, search by title/author/ISBN/genre), User Management (register, search by user ID/name), Borrowing and Returning (check availability, update status). Deliverables: Design Document, Source Code, User Manual, Test Cases.",
          "content": "",
          "pyqs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "artificial-intelligence-and-machine-learning-3-pbcst304-mModule 4-t30",
          "title": "Project Suggestion: Online Payment Processing System using OOP and Dynamic Polymorphism - Design and implement an Online Payment Processing System using Object-Oriented Programming principles in Java with a focus on dynamic polymorphism. Class Design: Payment (abstract base class), CreditCardPayment, PayPalPayment, BankTransferPayment (inherit from Payment), PaymentProcessor (manages and processes different payment types). Functionalities: Add Payment Method, Process Payment (demonstrate dynamic polymorphism). Deliverables: Design Document, Source Code, User Manual, Test Cases.",
